@startuml uc-inspect-members
!include _theme.iuml

state inspectMembers as "inspectMembers()" {

  state " " as RequestingInventory
  state " " as Listing
  state " " as Comparing

  [*] --> RequestingInventory
  note on link
  <b>Operator</b> asks who is in the organisation, and
  which of the people the configuration names are not
  end note

  RequestingInventory --> Listing
  note on link
  <b>Octoform</b> reads the owners, the members, the outside
  collaborators, and the invitations that are waiting or
  that failed
  • a pending invitation carries its age in whole days
  • a failed one carries GitHub's own reason
  end note

  Listing --> Comparing
  note on link
  <b>Octoform</b> collects every login the configuration
  names — team membership, role holders, repository
  collaborators — and subtracts everyone the
  organisation already knows
  • an outside collaborator counts as known
  • somebody already invited counts as asked
  end note

  Comparing --> [*]
  note on link
  <b>Operator</b> receives the four listings, the two-factor
  answer or the reason it is not visible, and the people
  the configuration names who are in no part of the
  organisation
  end note
}

inspectMembers --> CONFIGURATION_RESOLVED
note on link
read-only; nothing is invited, removed or
changed. A personal account has no members,
so the use case does not apply to one
end note
@enduml
